+// ---- RESEARCH PROTOTYPE (track exposure): local exposure + eye adaptation ----
+//
+// The frame is display-encoded. In the shipped (LDR) path it is already
+// tonemapped per fragment with the toe-less Neutral curve, which is identity
+// below 0.8 linear and exactly invertible above it (the curve keeps the max
+// channel at newPeak, so the peak and the desaturation weight can be solved
+// back), so the post pass recovers a scene-linear estimate up to ~5.6x. In the
+// HDR path (hdr=1, RGBA16F frame) the world shaders skip their tonemap and the
+// frame already holds display-encoded scene radiance.
